    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Ms Smith invested $\\$50\\,000$ at 6% p.a. interest, compounded annually, for four years. The tax department wants to know exactly how much interest she earned each year. Calculate these figures for Ms Smith. Give monetary answers to the nearest cent.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Year 1: $\\$3000.00$; year 2: $\\$3180.00$; year 3: $\\$3370.80$; year 4: $\\$3573.05$.",
      "worked": "Each year, interest is 6% of the balance at the start of that year.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}I_1&=50\\,000(0.06)=\\$3000.00\\\\I_2&=50\\,000(1.06)(0.06)=\\$3180.00\\\\I_3&=50\\,000(1.06)^2(0.06)=\\$3370.80\\\\I_4&=50\\,000(1.06)^3(0.06)\\approx\\$3573.05\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
